    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-floor offensive profile led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (75.38) and **Yordan Alvarez** (73.34). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns the top spot in our lineup today; his ability to exploit Landen Roupp, combined with a favorable batting order position, makes him an elite play, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains a core anchor despite a neutral park factor due to his superlative 0.454 xwOBA. **Trea Turner** (70.35) and **Kyle Schwarber** (68.40) also represent high-upside starts; **Trea Turner** specifically benefits from the slow delivery of Brandon Eisert, which significantly boosts his stolen base probability in a category where we remain hyper-aggressive.\n\nPlatoon advantages and environmental factors are shifting several decisions today. **Luke Raley** (64.85) is a high-value start against K. Montero, bolstered by a +13% adjustment for the pitcher's projected skill level and a meaningful +7% platoon edge. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (73.13) thrives today on park factors and a prime leadoff spot, assuming he maintains that position once lineups are finalized. The most difficult bench decision involved **Colt Keith** (55.09), who was the first cut from the starting nine; while his numbers were robust, he lost out to **Caleb Durbin** (56.08) because **Caleb Durbin** maintains a more consistent opportunity for counting stats in a better projected batting order slot, despite the relative strength of the opposing matchup.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that several hitters, including **Gary Sanchez**, **Chase Meidroth**, and **Junior Caminero**, are pending official lineup confirmation. While we have projected them based on historical data, these spots carry variance; should **Gary Sanchez** slide down the order, his efficiency score would likely regress. Furthermore, we are closely monitoring the matchup for **Dillon Dingler** (43.78) against B. Miller; while he is currently in the lineup, his low marginal score makes him the most volatile asset in our daily rotation, though he remains active to ensure we maximize our category coverage across the catcher position.",
